---

<div class="smg-header-collage" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<div class="smg-page">
  <section class="smg-hero" id="top">
    <div class="smg-hero__copy">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Vintage Gibson Specialist</p>
      <h1>Sell Your Vintage Gibson to a Buyer Who Knows What It Is</h1>
      <p class="smg-hero__lead">Vintage guitars have been at the center of my life for more than twelve years. I love learning where an old Gibson has been, who played it and the stories that stayed with it. Whether it's a Les Paul, an SG, an ES-335 or an old flat-top, send me a few photos and tell me what you know. I'll look it over myself and, if it's a guitar I can buy, make you a cash offer with no obligation.</p>
      <div class="smg-hero__actions">
        <Button href="#appraisal" variant="rust" size="lg">Fill Out the Form</Button>
        <a class="smg-button-secondary" href={hrefs.tel}>Call or Text Joe</a>
      </div>
      <a class="smg-hero__story-link" href="#owner-stories">Read Guitar Stories</a>
      <div class="smg-trust-row">
        <span>Insured Nationwide Shipping</span>
        <span>No Obligation</span>
        <span>Deal Directly With Joe</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="smg-hero__image">
      <LicensedImage src={heroGuitar} alt="Vintage 1957 Gibson Les Paul Goldtop handled by Joe's Vintage Guitars" width={950} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-proof" aria-label="Joe's experience">
    <div><strong>12+</strong><span>Years Buying Full-Time</span></div>
    <div><strong>10,000+</strong><span>Instruments Appraised</span></div>
    <div><strong>50</strong><span>States Bought From</span></div>
    <div><strong>2,100+</strong><span>Positive Reviews</span></div>
  </section>

  <span class="smg-anchor" id="receive-free-consultation"></span>
  <section class="smg-appraisal" id="appraisal">
    <div class="smg-appraisal__copy"><p class="smg-eyebrow">Talk With Me</p><h2>Tell Me About Your Gibson</h2><p>You don't need to know the model, year or value. Send me whatever photos you have and tell me anything you know about the guitar. I'll look it over myself and get back to you.</p><p>If you'd like to know the ideal photos to send, <a href="#photo-guide">read the six-photo guide</a>.</p><a href={hrefs.tel}>Call or Text {contact.phone}</a></div>
    <LeadForm formId="sell-my-gibson" instrumentMode="model-only" serial={{ label: "What does the serial number look like? Look on the back of the headstock or inside the body.", options: serialOptions }} submitLabel="Send" />
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-process" id="process">
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="how-to-sell-your-guitar"></span>
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="my-guitar-buying-process"></span>
    <header class="smg-heading">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">How It Works</p>
      <h2>Selling Your Gibson Doesn't Have to Be Complicated</h2>
      <p>You'll deal with me from the first message through payment. Here's what I need to get started.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="smg-steps">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Send Me Photos</h3><p>Take clear photos of the front, back, headstock, serial number and case. Please don't clean or repair the guitar first.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>I'll Look It Over</h3><p>I'll identify the guitar and check the details that affect its value. There's no charge for the appraisal.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>I'll Make an Offer</h3><p>If it's a guitar I can buy, I'll make you a cash offer. You're free to accept it or turn it down.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Agree On Shipping And Payment</h3><p>If you decide to sell, we'll agree on the shipping and payment method before the guitar moves.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-shipping" id="shipping">
    <div class="smg-shipping__intro">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Nationwide Shipping</p>
      <h2>A Simple, Proven Way to Ship Your Vintage Gibson</h2>
      <p>I'm on the road across the U.S. buying guitars and <a href="/sell-a-guitar-collection/">guitar collections</a>, so an in-person meeting may be possible. Otherwise, we can use the prepaid FedEx process.</p>
      <p>Sellers across the country have trusted me with valuable and sentimental guitars. If we can't meet in person, I explain the shipping process with the offer so you can consider everything before deciding.</p>
      <p>We agree on the shipping and payment details before the guitar moves, and I stay available throughout the process.</p>
      <div class="smg-shipping__included"><strong>There's no shipping cost to you.</strong> Through my special FedEx account, the box, professional packing, fully insured shipping and tracking are all provided at the FedEx location.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="smg-shipping__columns">
      <article><h3>What You Receive With the Offer</h3><ul><li>A clear explanation of the process</li><li>Shipping and insurance details</li><li>Your choice of payment method</li></ul></article>
      <article><h3>What I Handle if You Decide to Sell</h3><ul><li>Prepaid shipping arrangements</li><li>Transit coverage and tracking</li><li>Same-day payment in most cases</li></ul></article>
    </div>
    <div class="smg-shipping__evidence">
      <header><p class="smg-eyebrow">From Sellers Who Used the Process</p><h3>Read What Sellers Said</h3><p>These comments come from people who shipped guitars to me. Each one links to the original Google review.</p></header>
      <div class="smg-shipping__reviews">
        {shippingReviews.map((review) => (
          <a href={review.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="smg-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
            <blockquote>“{review.quote}”</blockquote>
            <strong>{review.name}</strong>
            <small>Read the Google Review</small>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-value" id="value">
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="how-much-is-my-gibson-guitar"></span>
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="find-out-gibson-really-worth"></span>
    <header class="smg-heading">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">What Goes Into My Offer</p>
      <h2>How Much Will You Pay for My Vintage Gibson?</h2>
      <p>My offers are among the highest you'll get from a dealer, but they'll sit a little below full retail because I take on the work and risk of reselling the guitar. Model and year, original parts, finish and color, condition and repairs, the case and paperwork, and ownership history all help determine what I can pay.</p>
      <p>Send me a few photos and I'll tell you what I can pay. If you'd rather research first, the guides below will help you understand the details I look at.</p>
      <a class="smg-appraisal-route" href="/free-appraisal/"><strong>Looking for an appraisal instead?</strong><span>Visit the Free Appraisal Page</span></a>
    </header>
    <div class="smg-value__grid">
      {values.map((item) => (
        <article>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={item.icon}></path></svg>
          <h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.body}</p>
          {item.link && <a class="smg-value-card__link" href={item.link}>{item.linkLabel}</a>}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="smg-section-link">For more detail, use my <a href="/vintage-gibson-les-paul-market-value-guide/">vintage Les Paul market value guide</a>, read how the <a href="/post/how-the-year-of-manufacture-of-your-vintage-gibson-guitar-affects-its-price/">year affects vintage Gibson value</a> or review <a href="/post/gibson-shipping-totals-1948-1979/">Gibson production totals</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-photo-guide" id="photo-guide">
    <div>
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">What To Send</p>
      <h2>Six Photos That Help Me Make An Accurate Offer</h2>
      <p>Clear, straight-on photos help me evaluate your Gibson and determine what I can pay. Use natural light, and don't remove pickups, open the electronics or take anything apart.</p>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li><span>01</span><strong>Full Front</strong><small>Include the entire body and headstock.</small></li>
      <li><span>02</span><strong>Full Back</strong><small>Show the neck, body and any wear or repairs.</small></li>
      <li><span>03</span><strong>Headstock Front</strong><small>Keep the logo, tuners and truss-rod cover in view.</small></li>
      <li><span>04</span><strong>Headstock Back</strong><small>Photograph the serial number and factory stamps clearly.</small></li>
      <li><span>05</span><strong>Bridge and Controls</strong><small>Show the pickups, knobs, bridge and tailpiece.</small></li>
      <li><span>06</span><strong>Case and Paperwork</strong><small>Include tags, receipts, old parts and family photos.</small></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

